@page "/help"

<PageTitle>Help · Configurator</PageTitle>
<h1>Help with configuration</h1>
<AppCard>
    <h2>Choose a definition</h2>
    <p>Use a bundled definition, browse the optional Definition Store or open a local JSON file.
        Public HTTPS source links are also supported. Select an exact revision; publisher names and Store inclusion do not authenticate a publisher.</p>
    <AppButton Href="open" Variant="Variant.Outlined">Open configuration</AppButton>
</AppCard>
<section>
    <h2>Keep control of your answers</h2>
    <p>Answers and prepared files stay in this tab. They are never saved in appearance preferences or public caches.
        Closing or reloading the tab clears them. Leaving a workspace asks you to discard your current work.</p>
    <p>Secret entry requires your consent for each workspace. Revoking consent clears secret answers and prepared output.
        A draft with deferred secrets still needs completion. Copying or downloading a file is a deliberate transfer to your chosen destination.</p>
    <p>Browser downloads cannot guarantee native restricted-file permissions. Your target application validates and authorizes application of the files.</p>
</section>
<section>
    <h2>Work offline</h2>
    <p>While online, use Open configuration to prepare the application for offline use.
        Only retain a definition after confirming it is safe public content. Cached definitions contain no saved answers.</p>
    <p>The Store is optional. A package without Store content still supports bundled definitions, local JSON files and public source links.</p>
</section>
<section>
    <h2>Adjust presentation</h2>
    <p>The header offers system, light, dark and high-contrast appearance and automatic, left-to-right or right-to-left direction.
        These preferences are local to your browser and do not change the configuration you are preparing.</p>
</section>
